[
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "# Edge to Cloud Broker Bridge — production TLS replacement\n\nThis optional notebook contains one executable production alternative. Run it on the **edge broker** instead of the `EdgeToCloudBridge` local demo Route in `edge-cloud-bridge.lotnb`. It does not replace the Models, Actions, or cloud Rules.\n\n## Safe deployment order\n\n1. On the cloud broker, create `bridge_site_plant` and deploy the solution notebook's Rules.\n2. Mount the CA and client certificate files into the edge broker container.\n3. Replace the example host and secret placeholders below through your deployment secret process.\n4. On the edge broker, deploy the solution Models and Actions.\n5. Run this TLS Route cell. Do not also run the local demo Route with the same site mapping.\n\nThe endpoint must be real and reachable. Roll back by removing/disabling `EdgeToCloudBridgeTls` and restoring the prior known-good Route definition."
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "Store the host **without** a URL scheme. Mount certs into the edge container and point the paths below at those files.\n\n> Requires a real TLS endpoint and certificates; skip in the local Compose demo."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ROUTE EdgeToCloudBridgeTls WITH TYPE MQTT_BRIDGE\n    ADD SOURCE_CONFIG\n        WITH BROKER SELF\n    ADD DESTINATION_CONFIG\n        WITH BROKER_ADDRESS \"cloud.example.com\"\n        WITH BROKER_PORT '8883'\n        WITH CLIENT_ID \"edge-site-plant-bridge-tls\"\n        WITH USERNAME \"bridge_site_plant\"\n        WITH PASSWORD \"CHANGE_ME_BRIDGE_PASSWORD\"\n        WITH USE_TLS \"true\"\n        WITH ALLOW_UNTRUSTED_CERTS \"false\"\n        WITH SERVER_CA_CERT_PATH \"/certs/ca.pem\"\n        WITH CLIENT_CERT_PATH \"/certs/client.pem\"\n        WITH CLIENT_CERT_PASS \"CHANGE_ME_CERT_PASS\"\n        WITH RECONNECTION_RETRIES '20'\n    ADD MAPPING siteFactoryOutTls\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"factory/#\"\n        WITH DESTINATION_TOPIC \"sites/site-plant/factory/#\"\n        WITH DIRECTION \"out\""
  }
]